-- The nightly rollup of the telemetry record (R2) that the fleet read and the operator's anomaly read come from. One row per install, account, and day: the day's batch and event counts, and its measures (docs/telemetry.md, "The report"). The day is the one the batch arrived (UTC), the same as its R2 key. A day is rolled up again by deleting its rows and writing them, so a second run changes nothing. It holds an install id and an account pseudonym because the floor is counted in installs; no read serves either, and nothing here joins to a deposit or reaches a bundle.
CREATE TABLE telemetry_install_days (day TEXT NOT NULL, install TEXT NOT NULL, account TEXT NOT NULL, batches INTEGER NOT NULL, events INTEGER NOT NULL, measures TEXT NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY (day, install, account));
